{# IN·09 — how serious this month's incidents are, the dimension a map pin cannot
   show.

   Severity is set when a ranger VERIFIES the report, not when it is filed — a
   raised alarm can be stood down once somebody has seen it — which is why the tab
   says "set at verification". One bar per level the model carries, most serious
   first so the eye lands on the worst of the month
   ({@see IncidentDashboard::severitiesWorstFirst}).

   The drawing is the chart layer's ({@see _charts.html.twig}); this partial reads
   the count at each level and hands over labelled bars. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiIncident/dashboard/_charts.html.twig' as charts %}
<div class="c chartcard" data-w="severity">
    <span class="tab">By severity<span class="src">{% if dashboard.filter.from %}· {{ dashboard.filter.from|date('F Y')|lower }} {% endif %}· set at verification</span></span>
    {% set bars = [] %}
    {% for level in dashboard.severitiesWorstFirst %}
        {% set bars = bars|merge([{
            label: level.label,
            value: dashboard.severityCount(level),
            title: level.label ~ ': ' ~ dashboard.severityCount(level),
        }]) %}
    {% endfor %}
    {{ charts.bars(bars) }}
</div>
